IMPORT prelude

-- Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018 (Singapore) -- Parts 1 and 2: the groups of
-- public body, who can be directed and how, and the data-sharing offences.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 August
-- 2026, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PSGA2018.txt
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. A citation count across the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this
-- repository found 70 Acts that cite the Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018, for an
-- Act of only 84,000 characters, so it is the best ratio of reach to size among the
-- unencoded Acts. Most of those citations are to ss 4 and 5, the Minister's power to
-- direct a statutory board, which is why Part 2 is encoded in full.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules
-- skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the content of the three Schedules (which public body is in which
-- Part), taken as a fact supplied about each body; s 2(1) definitions that are plain
-- cross-references; s 3 (purposes); ss 43 and 44.

§ `Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018 -- Parts 1 and 2`

§§ `2(1) -- what a "public body" is, and which Group it falls in`

-- s 2(1): "'public body' means a body corporate established by a public Act for the
-- purposes of a public function but EXCLUDES A TOWN COUNCIL established under section 4
-- of the Town Councils Act 1988."
--
-- The groups. Read the definitions carefully, because they are not parallel:
--   "Group 1 public body" = a public body specified in the First Schedule.
--   "Group 1A / 1B / 1C" = a public body specified in Part 1 / 2 / 3 of the First Schedule.
--   "Group 2 public body" = a public body specified in the Second Schedule, BEING A
--       PUBLIC BODY THE MAIN FUNCTION OF WHICH IS TO REGULATE THE PRACTICE AND
--       STANDARDS OF A PROFESSION.
--   "Group 2A / 2B" = a public body specified in Part 1 / 2 of the Second Schedule.
--   "Group 3 public body" = a public body specified in the Third Schedule, BEING A
--       PUBLIC BODY THE MAIN FUNCTION OF WHICH IS TO REPRESENT PARTICULAR COMMUNITY
--       INTERESTS OR THE VOLUNTEER MOVEMENT.
--   "Group 3A / 3B" = a public body specified in Part 1 / 2 of the Third Schedule.
--
-- So Group 2 and Group 3 carry a main-function condition that Group 1 does not and that
-- Groups 2A, 2B, 3A and 3B do not repeat. A body listed in Part 1 of the Second
-- Schedule whose main function is NOT regulating a profession is a Group 2A public body
-- and not a Group 2 public body. Part 3 (s 12) and Part 4 (s 22) apply to "every
-- Group 1, every Group 2 and every Group 3", so such a body falls outside them even
-- though s 15 names Group 2A. The Schedule lists are carried as a fact about each body.
--
-- The First Schedule's Part 2 (Group 1B) lists the Defence Science and Technology
-- Agency alone, and Part 3 (Group 1C) the People's Association alone.
DECLARE ScheduleListing IS ONE OF
    `Part 1 of the First Schedule`
    `Part 2 of the First Schedule`
    `Part 3 of the First Schedule`
    `Part 1 of the Second Schedule`
    `Part 2 of the Second Schedule`
    `Part 1 of the Third Schedule`
    `Part 2 of the Third Schedule`
    `no Schedule`

DECLARE BodyFacts HAS
    `a body corporate established by a public Act for the purposes of a public function` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Town Council established under section 4 of the Town Councils Act 1988` IS A BOOLEAN
    `listed in` IS A ScheduleListing
    `its main function is to regulate the practice and standards of a profession` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its main function is to represent particular community interests or the volunteer movement` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a public body` IF
        `the body`'s `a body corporate established by a public Act for the purposes of a public function`
    AND NOT `the body`'s `a Town Council established under section 4 of the Town Councils Act 1988`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a Group 1A public body` IF
        `the body is a public body` `the body`
    AND `the body`'s `listed in` EQUALS `Part 1 of the First Schedule`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a Group 1B public body` IF
        `the body is a public body` `the body`
    AND `the body`'s `listed in` EQUALS `Part 2 of the First Schedule`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a Group 1C public body` IF
        `the body is a public body` `the body`
    AND `the body`'s `listed in` EQUALS `Part 3 of the First Schedule`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a Group 1 public body` IF
        `the body is a Group 1A public body` `the body`
    OR  `the body is a Group 1B public body` `the body`
    OR  `the body is a Group 1C public body` `the body`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a Group 2A public body` IF
        `the body is a public body` `the body`
    AND `the body`'s `listed in` EQUALS `Part 1 of the Second Schedule`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a Group 2B public body` IF
        `the body is a public body` `the body`
    AND `the body`'s `listed in` EQUALS `Part 2 of the Second Schedule`

-- Group 2 itself carries the main-function condition.
GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a Group 2 public body` IF
        (    `the body is a Group 2A public body` `the body`
         OR  `the body is a Group 2B public body` `the body`)
    AND `the body`'s `its main function is to regulate the practice and standards of a profession`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a Group 3A public body` IF
        `the body is a public body` `the body`
    AND `the body`'s `listed in` EQUALS `Part 1 of the Third Schedule`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a Group 3B public body` IF
        `the body is a public body` `the body`
    AND `the body`'s `listed in` EQUALS `Part 2 of the Third Schedule`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a Group 3 public body` IF
        (    `the body is a Group 3A public body` `the body`
         OR  `the body is a Group 3B public body` `the body`)
    AND `the body`'s `its main function is to represent particular community interests or the volunteer movement`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a Group 1, 2 or 3 public body` IF
        `the body is a Group 1 public body` `the body`
    OR  `the body is a Group 2 public body` `the body`
    OR  `the body is a Group 3 public body` `the body`

§§ `2(1) "Singapore public sector agency"`

-- s 2(1): "'Singapore public sector agency' means any of the following:
--   (a) a Group 1, Group 2 or Group 3 public body;
--   (b) a ministry or department of the Government;
--   (c) an Organ of State;
--   (d) a public officer or a person exercising a public official function, who is
--       declared by the Minister by order in the Gazette to be a Singapore public
--       sector agency for the purposes of this Act."
--
-- A Town Council is not a public body and so not an agency under (a); it is one only if
-- the Minister declares it under (d), and (d) speaks of "a public officer or a person
-- exercising a public official function", which a body corporate does not obviously fit.
DECLARE AgencyFacts HAS
    `the body` IS A BodyFacts
    `a ministry or department of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an Organ of State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared by the Minister by order in the Gazette to be a Singapore public sector agency` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the agency` IS AN AgencyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this is a Singapore public sector agency` IF
        `the body is a Group 1, 2 or 3 public body` (`the agency`'s `the body`)
    OR  `the agency`'s `a ministry or department of the Government`
    OR  `the agency`'s `an Organ of State`
    OR  `the agency`'s `declared by the Minister by order in the Gazette to be a Singapore public sector agency`

§§ `2(2), 7(7) -- officers, and "relevant public official"`

-- s 2(2): "an individual is an officer of a Singapore public sector agency for the time he
-- or she is --
--   (a) a public officer holding a post in a ministry or department of the Government or
--       an Organ of State which is that agency (including a public officer on LEAVE
--       WITHOUT PAY);
--   (b) an EMPLOYEE of a Group 1, Group 2 or Group 3 public body which is that agency
--       (including an employee on leave without pay); or
--   (c) under a SECONDMENT arrangement making available temporarily to that agency the
--       service of the individual."
-- s 7(7): "'relevant public official', for a Singapore public sector agency, means --
--   (a) an officer of the agency;
--   (b) a member of a Group 1, Group 2 or Group 3 public body which is that agency, or of
--       the governing body of such a public body; or
--   (c) the chief executive of a Group 1, Group 2 or Group 3 public body which is that
--       agency."
--
-- "For the time he or she is": status is tested at the moment of the conduct. s 7(1)(c)
-- and s 8(1)(c) repeat "at the time of the disclosure" and "at the time of taking that
-- action", so a person who has left is not a relevant public official however recently.
-- A person on leave without pay is, and a contractor's employee is not.
DECLARE PersonFacts HAS
    `a public officer holding a post in the ministry, department or Organ of State, including on leave without pay` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an employee of the Group 1, 2 or 3 public body, including on leave without pay` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under a secondment arrangement making the individual's service available to the agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a member of the public body or of its governing body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the chief executive of the public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a contractor supplying goods or services to the agency or to another agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an employee of such a contractor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the time of the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A PersonFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an officer of the agency` IF
        `the person`'s `at the time of the conduct`
    AND (    `the person`'s `a public officer holding a post in the ministry, department or Organ of State, including on leave without pay`
         OR  `the person`'s `an employee of the Group 1, 2 or 3 public body, including on leave without pay`
         OR  `the person`'s `under a secondment arrangement making the individual's service available to the agency`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A PersonFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a relevant public official` IF
        `the person`'s `at the time of the conduct`
    AND (    `the person is an officer of the agency` `the person`
         OR  `the person`'s `a member of the public body or of its governing body`
         OR  `the person`'s `the chief executive of the public body`)

§§ `2(3) -- "control" of information`

-- s 2(3): an agency "is taken to have control of information if -- (a) the agency has
-- possession or custody of the information; or (b) the agency has the information in the
-- possession or custody of SOME OTHER PERSON."
--
-- So information held for an agency by a contractor (a cloud host, a mailing house) is
-- under the agency's control.
GIVEN `the agency has possession or custody of the information` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the information is in the possession or custody of some other person on the agency's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the information is under the agency's control` IF
        `the agency has possession or custody of the information`
    OR  `the information is in the possession or custody of some other person on the agency's behalf`

§§ `4 -- directions for a whole-of-government approach`

-- s 4(1): "the Minister may, on the recommendation of the relevant Minister (if any), give
-- or jointly give a direction -- (a) to all Singapore public sector agencies; or (b) to a
-- Singapore public sector agency or a class of them specified in the direction, requiring
-- [them] to comply with a POLICY OF THE GOVERNMENT ... relating to all or any pertinent
-- subject matter."
-- s 4(2): "A direction ... may be made ONLY for all or any of the following purposes: (a) to
-- uphold and promote the values of the Singapore public sector; (b) to secure economies or
-- efficiencies; (c) to improve the efficiency or effectiveness of policies, programme
-- management or service planning and delivery ...; (d) to ensure business continuity;
-- (e) to ensure accountable and prudent stewardship of ... finances and resources; (f) to
-- manage risks to the financial position of the Government; (g) to support a
-- whole-of-government approach".
-- s 4(3): "'pertinent subject matter' means (a) employment, management and discipline of
-- employees; (b) management of official documents; (c) financial and resource management
-- and accountability; (d) use or development of information technology; (e) data
-- governance (including personal data protection) and sharing of information ...".
-- s 4(4): the "relevant Minister" for each of (a) to (e) is the Minister responsible for,
-- respectively, public sector personnel policy; Government records and archives;
-- Government finance; public sector information-communications technology and related
-- engineering; and public sector data governance.
--
-- s 4 reaches EVERY Singapore public sector agency: Groups 1, 2 and 3, ministries,
-- departments and Organs of State. s 5 below reaches only Group 1.
DECLARE PertinentSubjectMatter IS ONE OF
    `employment, management and discipline of employees`
    `management of official documents`
    `financial and resource management and accountability`
    `use or development of information technology`
    `data governance and sharing of information between agencies`
    `something else`

DECLARE RelevantMinister IS ONE OF
    `the Minister responsible for public sector personnel policy`
    `the Minister responsible for Government records and archives`
    `the Minister responsible for Government finance`
    `the Minister responsible for public sector information-communications technology and related engineering`
    `the Minister responsible for public sector data governance`
    `no relevant Minister`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A PertinentSubjectMatter
GIVETH A RelevantMinister
DECIDE `the relevant Minister for the subject matter` IS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `employment, management and discipline of employees` THEN `the Minister responsible for public sector personnel policy`
    WHEN `management of official documents` THEN `the Minister responsible for Government records and archives`
    WHEN `financial and resource management and accountability` THEN `the Minister responsible for Government finance`
    WHEN `use or development of information technology` THEN `the Minister responsible for public sector information-communications technology and related engineering`
    WHEN `data governance and sharing of information between agencies` THEN `the Minister responsible for public sector data governance`
    OTHERWISE `no relevant Minister`

DECLARE DirectionFacts HAS
    `given by the Minister, or jointly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the recommendation of the relevant Minister, where there is one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `requires compliance with a policy of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the subject matter` IS A PertinentSubjectMatter
    `to uphold and promote the values of the Singapore public sector` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to secure economies or efficiencies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to improve the efficiency or effectiveness of policies, programme management or service planning and delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to ensure business continuity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to ensure accountable and prudent stewardship of finances and resources` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to manage risks to the financial position of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to support a whole-of-government approach` IS A BOOLEAN
    `inconsistent with the Act or another written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `would impede a statutorily independent function` IS A BOOLEAN
    `would impede a quasi-judicial function in relation to a particular matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `requires a particular act or result in respect of a particular person or persons` IS A BOOLEAN
    `requires an employment decision relating to a particular individual` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the direction` IS A DirectionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the direction serves one of the seven permitted purposes` IF
        `the direction`'s `to uphold and promote the values of the Singapore public sector`
    OR  `the direction`'s `to secure economies or efficiencies`
    OR  `the direction`'s `to improve the efficiency or effectiveness of policies, programme management or service planning and delivery`
    OR  `the direction`'s `to ensure business continuity`
    OR  `the direction`'s `to ensure accountable and prudent stewardship of finances and resources`
    OR  `the direction`'s `to manage risks to the financial position of the Government`
    OR  `the direction`'s `to support a whole-of-government approach`

GIVEN `the direction` IS A DirectionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the subject matter is pertinent` IF
    CONSIDER `the direction`'s `the subject matter`
    WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 11(3): "This Part does not authorise any Minister to direct ... requiring -- (a) the
-- performance or non-performance of a particular act or the bringing about of a particular
-- result, in respect of a particular person or persons; or (b) the making of an employment
-- decision relating to a particular individual."
--
-- Both limbs are about particulars. A direction that every agency do X is within the
-- power; one that this agency do X to this person is not. s 11(5) defines "employment
-- decision" to include appointment, promotion, transfer, remuneration, termination and
-- disciplinary action, so the Minister cannot direct a particular dismissal, although
-- he may direct a policy on dismissals, being "employment, management and discipline of
-- employees" under s 4(3)(a).
GIVEN `the direction` IS A DirectionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11(3) takes the direction outside the Minister's power` IF
        `the direction`'s `requires a particular act or result in respect of a particular person or persons`
    OR  `the direction`'s `requires an employment decision relating to a particular individual`

GIVEN `the direction` IS A DirectionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4 empowers the direction` IF
        `the direction`'s `given by the Minister, or jointly`
    AND `the direction`'s `on the recommendation of the relevant Minister, where there is one`
    AND `the direction`'s `requires compliance with a policy of the Government`
    AND `the direction serves one of the seven permitted purposes` `the direction`
    AND `the subject matter is pertinent` `the direction`
    AND NOT `section 11(3) takes the direction outside the Minister's power` `the direction`
    AND NOT `the direction`'s `inconsistent with the Act or another written law`

-- s 11(2): a direction "is not binding on a Singapore public sector agency TO THE EXTENT
-- (if any) to which it would impede or affect the performance of (a) a statutorily
-- independent function ...; or (b) a quasi-judicial function ... in relation to a
-- particular matter." The direction is therefore valid and partly non-binding: it is cut
-- back, not struck down.
GIVEN `the direction` IS A DirectionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the direction binds the agency in full` IF
        `section 4 empowers the direction` `the direction`
    AND NOT `the direction`'s `would impede a statutorily independent function`
    AND NOT `the direction`'s `would impede a quasi-judicial function in relation to a particular matter`

GIVEN `the direction` IS A DirectionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the direction binds the agency in part` IF
        `section 4 empowers the direction` `the direction`
    AND (    `the direction`'s `would impede a statutorily independent function`
         OR  `the direction`'s `would impede a quasi-judicial function in relation to a particular matter`)

§§ `5 -- directions by the responsible Minister`

-- s 5(1): "The responsible Minister for a GROUP 1 public body may give to the public body
-- directions as to the performance by the public body of its functions."
-- s 5(2): this does not affect any requirement in the constitutional Act "requiring the
-- responsible Minister to consult any person specified in that Act before exercising the
-- power".
--
-- The power is confined to Group 1 and is not confined to any purpose or subject matter,
-- beyond s 11. A Group 2 or Group 3 body cannot be given a s 5 direction (it can be given
-- a s 4 direction), and a body that is in Group 2A and fails the main-function test is
-- neither.
GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts, `the consultation the constitutional Act requires has been carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 5 direction may be given to the body` IF
        `the body is a Group 1 public body` `the body`
    AND `the consultation the constitutional Act requires has been carried out`

§§ `6 -- authority to share`

-- s 6(1): "Where a data sharing direction is given to a Singapore public sector agency --
-- (a) the agency and every officer of that agency; and (b) where the agency is a public
-- body, the members of the public body, are authorised to share the information under the
-- control of the agency with another Singapore public sector agency to the extent
-- permitted by the data sharing direction DESPITE ANY OBLIGATION AS TO CONFIDENTIALITY
-- UNDER THE COMMON LAW."
-- s 6(2): "subsection (1) does not override any obligation as to confidentiality because
-- of LEGAL PRIVILEGE OR CONTRACT."
-- s 6(3): "this Act is not intended to prevent or discourage the sharing of information by
-- agencies as permitted or required by or under any Act or other law (apart from this Act)."
-- s 2(1): a "data sharing direction" is a direction "given under SECTION 4".
--
-- What s 6 overrides is the COMMON LAW of confidence and nothing else. It does not
-- override legal privilege or contract (s 6(2)); and it says nothing about a statutory
-- secrecy provision in another Act, which is therefore untouched. A direction under s 5
-- is not a data sharing direction and authorises nothing under s 6.
DECLARE ConfidentialityObligation IS ONE OF
    `a duty of confidence at common law`
    `legal privilege`
    `a contractual obligation of confidentiality`
    `a statutory secrecy provision in another Act`
    `no obligation at all`

GIVEN `the obligation` IS A ConfidentialityObligation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6(1) overrides the obligation` IF
    CONSIDER `the obligation`
    WHEN `a duty of confidence at common law` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE SharingFacts HAS
    `a data sharing direction has been given under section 4 to the agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person sharing is the agency, one of its officers, or a member of the public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the recipient is another Singapore public sector agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sharing is within the extent the direction permits` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the obligation standing in the way` IS A ConfidentialityObligation

GIVEN `the sharing` IS A SharingFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6 authorises the sharing` IF
        `the sharing`'s `a data sharing direction has been given under section 4 to the agency`
    AND `the sharing`'s `the person sharing is the agency, one of its officers, or a member of the public body`
    AND `the sharing`'s `the recipient is another Singapore public sector agency`
    AND `the sharing`'s `the sharing is within the extent the direction permits`

-- Authorised, and free of the obstacle? The authorisation exists whatever the obstacle;
-- the question is whether this particular obligation survives it.
GIVEN `the sharing` IS A SharingFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the obligation no longer stands in the way` IF
        `section 6 authorises the sharing` `the sharing`
    AND (    `section 6(1) overrides the obligation` (`the sharing`'s `the obligation standing in the way`)
         OR  `the sharing`'s `the obligation standing in the way` EQUALS `no obligation at all`)

§§ `7 -- unauthorised disclosure and improper use`

-- All three offences carry: a fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 2 years or both. ss 7(1), 7(3), 7(4) and 8(1).
`the maximum fine for the offences in sections 7 and 8, in dollars` MEANS 5000
`the maximum imprisonment for the offences in sections 7 and 8, in months` MEANS 24

-- s 7(1): "If -- (a) an individual discloses, or the individual's conduct causes disclosure
-- of, information under the control of a Singapore public sector agency to another person
-- (whether or not a Singapore public sector agency); (b) the disclosure is NOT AUTHORISED
-- BY ANY DATA SHARING DIRECTION given to the agency; (c) the individual is a RELEVANT PUBLIC
-- OFFICIAL of the agency at the time of the disclosure; and (d) the individual does so
-- (i) KNOWING that the disclosure is not in accordance with that direction; or (ii)
-- RECKLESS as to whether it is or is not, the individual shall be guilty of an offence".
--
-- There is NO requirement of gain, harm or loss. The disclosure is the offence.
--
-- s 7(2): "it is a defence for the defendant to PROVE, on a balance of probabilities, any
-- of the following: (a) the information was, at the time of its disclosure by the
-- defendant, GENERALLY AVAILABLE INFORMATION; (b) the defendant disclosed ... (i) as
-- PERMITTED OR REQUIRED by or under an Act or other law (apart from this Act); (ii) as
-- authorised or required by an ORDER OF COURT; or (iii) in any other circumstances, or for
-- any other purpose, PRESCRIBED."
-- s 7(7): "'generally available information' means information that consists of readily
-- observable matter, including ... deductions, conclusions or inferences made or drawn from
-- readily observable matter".
-- s 7(7): "'disclose' includes provide access to information".
--
-- The burden of the defences is on the defendant. Note what the structure does to an
-- ordinary official going about ordinary work: the offence is framed against data sharing
-- directions, so an official's routine disclosure that no direction authorises satisfies
-- element (b), and it is for the official to prove it was permitted by another law.
DECLARE DefenceFacts HAS
    `the defendant proves the information was generally available at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defendant proves the act was permitted or required by or under an Act or other law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defendant proves the act was authorised or required by an order of court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defendant proves the act was in circumstances or for a purpose prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the defences` IS A DefenceFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a defence under section 7(2) or (5) is proved` IF
        `the defences`'s `the defendant proves the information was generally available at the time`
    OR  `the defences`'s `the defendant proves the act was permitted or required by or under an Act or other law`
    OR  `the defences`'s `the defendant proves the act was authorised or required by an order of court`
    OR  `the defences`'s `the defendant proves the act was in circumstances or for a purpose prescribed`

DECLARE DisclosureFacts HAS
    `the person` IS A PersonFacts
    `disclosed information, or caused its disclosure, to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information is under the control of the agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure was authorised by a data sharing direction given to the agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew the disclosure was not in accordance with that direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was reckless as to whether it was in accordance with that direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defences` IS A DefenceFacts

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DisclosureFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the elements of section 7(1) are made out` IF
        `the facts`'s `disclosed information, or caused its disclosure, to another person`
    AND `the facts`'s `the information is under the control of the agency`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the disclosure was authorised by a data sharing direction given to the agency`
    AND `the person is a relevant public official` (`the facts`'s `the person`)
    AND (    `the facts`'s `knew the disclosure was not in accordance with that direction`
         OR  `the facts`'s `was reckless as to whether it was in accordance with that direction`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DisclosureFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` IF
        `the elements of section 7(1) are made out` `the facts`
    AND NOT `a defence under section 7(2) or (5) is proved` (`the facts`'s `the defences`)

-- s 7(3): use of information, by a relevant public official of the agency OR OF ANOTHER
-- agency, with a result. The four elements are: use not authorised by any data sharing
-- direction to A; relevant public official of A or another agency at the time; knowing or
-- reckless that the use is not in accordance with such a direction; and, as a result,
-- (i) a gain for the individual or another person, (ii) harm to another individual, or
-- (iii) a loss to another person.
-- s 7(7): "gain" is a gain in property or services (temporary or permanent) or an
-- opportunity to earn remuneration or a financial advantage; "harm" is physical harm or
-- harassment, alarm or distress; "loss" is a loss in property or services or of such an
-- opportunity, "but excludes, in relation to an individual, THE LOSS OF PERSONAL DATA about
-- the individual".
--
-- THE LOSS DEFINITION EXCLUDES WHAT THE OFFENCE IS MOST OFTEN ABOUT. An official who misuses
-- someone's personal data and thereby causes them only the loss of that personal data has
-- caused no "loss" within the section. They must have caused a gain, or harm (which
-- includes harassment, alarm or distress), or a loss of some other thing.
DECLARE UseFacts HAS
    `the person` IS A PersonFacts
    `made use of information under the control of an agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the use was authorised by a data sharing direction given to the agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew the use was not in accordance with such a direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was reckless as to whether it was in accordance with such a direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obtained a gain for the individual or another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused harm to another individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused a loss to another person other than the loss of that person's own personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only loss caused was the loss of the individual's own personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defences` IS A DefenceFacts

GIVEN `the facts` IS A UseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a result within section 7(3)(e) followed` IF
        `the facts`'s `obtained a gain for the individual or another person`
    OR  `the facts`'s `caused harm to another individual`
    OR  `the facts`'s `caused a loss to another person other than the loss of that person's own personal data`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A UseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 7(3) is committed` IF
        `the facts`'s `made use of information under the control of an agency`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the use was authorised by a data sharing direction given to the agency`
    AND `the person is a relevant public official` (`the facts`'s `the person`)
    AND (    `the facts`'s `knew the use was not in accordance with such a direction`
         OR  `the facts`'s `was reckless as to whether it was in accordance with such a direction`)
    AND `a result within section 7(3)(e) followed` `the facts`
    AND NOT `a defence under section 7(2) or (5) is proved` (`the facts`'s `the defences`)

-- s 7(4): the contractor's offence. "If -- (a) an individual makes use of information
-- (OTHER THAN PERSONAL DATA) under the control of a Singapore public sector agency (A); (b)
-- the use is not authorised BY A; (c) the individual is (i) a CONTRACTOR supplying goods or
-- services to A or to another agency; or (ii) an EMPLOYEE of a person who is such a
-- contractor; (d) the individual does so knowing or reckless that the use is not authorised
-- by A; and (e) the individual, as a result of that use, obtains a gain, causes harm, or
-- causes a loss".
--
-- COMPARE s 7(3):
--   * the contractor's offence EXCLUDES PERSONAL DATA entirely;
--   * the authorisation tested is A's, not a data sharing direction;
--   * and there is NO contractor's offence of DISCLOSURE at all: s 7(1) is confined to
--     relevant public officials, and a contractor's employee is not one.
-- So a contractor's employee who passes government personal data to a third party commits
-- no offence under this Act, whatever they gain.
DECLARE ContractorUseFacts HAS
    `the person` IS A PersonFacts
    `made use of information under the control of an agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information is personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the use was authorised by the agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew the use was not authorised by the agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was reckless as to whether it was authorised by the agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obtained a gain for the individual or another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused harm to another individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused a loss to another person other than the loss of that person's own personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defences` IS A DefenceFacts

GIVEN `the person` IS A PersonFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a contractor or a contractor's employee within section 7(4)(c)` IF
        `the person`'s `at the time of the conduct`
    AND (    `the person`'s `a contractor supplying goods or services to the agency or to another agency`
         OR  `the person`'s `an employee of such a contractor`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A ContractorUseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 7(4) is committed` IF
        `the facts`'s `made use of information under the control of an agency`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the information is personal data`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the use was authorised by the agency`
    AND `the person is a contractor or a contractor's employee within section 7(4)(c)` (`the facts`'s `the person`)
    AND (    `the facts`'s `knew the use was not authorised by the agency`
         OR  `the facts`'s `was reckless as to whether it was authorised by the agency`)
    AND (    `the facts`'s `obtained a gain for the individual or another person`
         OR  `the facts`'s `caused harm to another individual`
         OR  `the facts`'s `caused a loss to another person other than the loss of that person's own personal data`)
    AND NOT `a defence under section 7(2) or (5) is proved` (`the facts`'s `the defences`)

-- s 7(6): "subsection (2) or (5) does not affect any obligation or limitation imposed on,
-- or prohibition of, the disclosure or use of information ... by or under any other written
-- law or other law." A defence under this Act is not a defence under any other law.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a defence under section 7 is a defence under every other law` IF
    FALSE

§§ `8 -- unauthorised re-identification`

-- s 8(1): "If -- (a) an individual takes any action to RE-IDENTIFY or cause re-identification
-- of the person to whom ANONYMISED information under the control of a Singapore public sector
-- agency relates; (b) the re-identification is not authorised by any data sharing direction
-- given to the agency; (c) the individual is a relevant public official of the agency at the
-- time of taking that action; and (d) the individual does so knowing, or reckless as to
-- whether, the re-identification is not authorised by that direction".
--
-- As with s 7(1), there is no requirement of gain, harm or loss. s 8(2): the defences, which
-- the accused must PROVE on the balance of probabilities: (a) the information on the identity
-- is publicly available; (b) the action is permitted or required by or under an Act or other
-- law, authorised or required by court order, or in prescribed circumstances; or (c) the
-- accused (i) REASONABLY BELIEVED the re-identification was for a SPECIFIED PURPOSE (a purpose
-- in the Eleventh Schedule to the Personal Data Protection Act 2012), AND (ii) NOTIFIED
-- either the agency or the Government Technology Agency AS SOON AS WAS PRACTICABLE.
--
-- Limb (c) needs both halves: a reasonable belief that the purpose was specified is not
-- enough without prompt notification.
DECLARE ReidentificationFacts HAS
    `the person` IS A PersonFacts
    `took action to re-identify, or caused re-identification of, the person to whom anonymised information relates` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the re-identification was authorised by a data sharing direction given to the agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew the re-identification was not authorised by that direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was reckless as to whether it was authorised by that direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused proves the information on the identity is publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused proves the action was permitted or required by law, authorised by court order, or in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused proves they reasonably believed the re-identification was for a specified purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused proves they notified the agency or the Government Technology Agency as soon as was practicable` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A ReidentificationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a defence under section 8(2) is proved` IF
        `the facts`'s `the accused proves the information on the identity is publicly available`
    OR  `the facts`'s `the accused proves the action was permitted or required by law, authorised by court order, or in prescribed circumstances`
    OR  (    `the facts`'s `the accused proves they reasonably believed the re-identification was for a specified purpose`
         AND `the facts`'s `the accused proves they notified the agency or the Government Technology Agency as soon as was practicable`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A ReidentificationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 8(1) is committed` IF
        `the facts`'s `took action to re-identify, or caused re-identification of, the person to whom anonymised information relates`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the re-identification was authorised by a data sharing direction given to the agency`
    AND `the person is a relevant public official` (`the facts`'s `the person`)
    AND (    `the facts`'s `knew the re-identification was not authorised by that direction`
         OR  `the facts`'s `was reckless as to whether it was authorised by that direction`)
    AND NOT `a defence under section 8(2) is proved` `the facts`

§§ `9, 10, 11 -- the form, effect and limits of directions`

-- s 9(1): a direction under s 4 or 5 may be "in the form of a circular or an instruction or
-- order" addressed to the agency and, for a public body, to its members and chief executive,
-- and may be amended or replaced in the same way. s 9(2): "A direction ... DOES NOT HAVE
-- LEGISLATIVE EFFECT."
-- s 10(1): every agency to which a direction is given "must, in performing its functions,
-- comply with the direction starting from the date specified in the direction".
-- s 10(2): "The functions of a public body under written law are to be regarded as
-- INCLUDING compliance with a direction given to it".
-- s 11(1): a direction "must not be inconsistent with this Act or any other written law".
--
-- A direction binds the agency without being law. A direction that conflicts with a statute
-- fails s 11(1), and s 10(2) makes compliance one of the body's functions, so a body that
-- complies is acting within its functions even where the direction is not law.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a direction under section 4 or 5 has legislative effect` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `the date specified in the direction has been reached` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agency must comply` IF
    `the date specified in the direction has been reached`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compliance with a direction is one of the body's functions under written law` IF
    `the body is a public body` `the body`
